## 5. Installation guide

### Prerequisites

| Requirement | Version | How to check |
|-------------|---------|--------------|
| Go | 1.25 or later | `go version` |
| Git (optional) | any | `git --version` |

> The SQLite driver used by this project is pure Go — **no C compiler or external SQLite
> installation is required.**

### Step 1 — Get the code

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url> powersmart-kenya
cd powersmart-kenya
```

### Step 2 — Configure the backend

```bash
cd backend
cp .env.example .env
```

### Step 3 — Set required environment values

Open `.env` and set at minimum:

```env
APP_ENV=development
PORT=8080
JWT_SECRET=<at-least-32-random-characters>
```

Generate a secret:

```bash
openssl rand -hex 32
```

### Step 4 — (Recommended) Configure an admin account

Add to `.env` (the account is created automatically on first start):

```env
ADMIN_NAME=Super Administrator
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=<a-strong-unique-password>
```

### Step 5 — Build

```bash
cd backend
go build -o powersmart .
```

This produces a single executable, `powersmart`, in the `backend/` folder.

### Step 6 — Run

```bash
./powersmart
# or during development:
go run .
```

### Step 7 — Verify

Open `http://localhost:8080/api/health` in a browser — it should return:

```json
{"status":"success","message":"Backend is running"}
```

