## 7. Running the project

### Development

```bash
cd backend
go run .
```

### Production-style

```bash
cd backend
go build -o powersmart .
APP_ENV=production PORT=8080 JWT_SECRET=<secret> ./powersmart
```

> In production, also set `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to your domain(s) and run behind a reverse
> proxy (nginx/Caddy) that terminates TLS.

### Running the optional React prototype (developers only)

The React app under `frontend/src/` is a separate prototype and is **not** served by the Go
backend. To develop it in isolation:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev          # starts Vite on http://localhost:3000
```

