## 9. API reference

Base URL: `http://localhost:8080/api`

### 9.1 Health

**`GET /health`**

```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/api/health
```

Response:

```json
{"status":"success","message":"Backend is running"}
```

### 9.2 Authentication

**`POST /auth/register`** — create a tenant/landlord account.

Request:

```json
{
  "name": "Emma Jane",
  "email": "emma@example.com",
  "phone": "0712345678",
  "password": "StrongPass1",
  "meter_account": "1234567890",
  "role": "tenant"
}
```

`role` is optional; allowed values: `tenant` (default), `landlord`.

Response `201 Created`:

```json
{
  "token": "<jwt>",
  "user": {
    "id": "...",
    "name": "Emma Jane",
    "email": "emma@example.com",
    "phone": "0712345678",
    "meter_account": "1234567890",
    "meter_number": "KPM1234567890",
    "role": "tenant",
    "created_at": "..."
  }
}
```

**`POST /auth/login`** — sign in with any account.

Request: `{ "email": "...", "password": "..." }` → same response shape as register.

**`POST /auth/admin-login`** — admin-only sign in.

Same request shape as login. Returns `403` if the account is not an admin.

**`GET /auth/me`** *(protected)* — current profile.

```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**`POST /auth/logout`** *(protected)* — stateless session discard.

### 9.3 Meter

All protected.

| Method | Path | Body / Notes |
|--------|------|--------------|
| GET | `/meter` | Current meter state |
| POST | `/meter/telemetry` | `{ "units_remaining": 24.5 }` |
| GET | `/meter/prediction` | Depletion forecast |
| PUT | `/meter/settings` | `{ "auto_topup": true, "topup_threshold": 5, "topup_amount_ksh": 500 }` |

Example prediction response:

```json
{
  "units_remaining": 24.5,
  "daily_avg_units": 3.4,
  "days_remaining": 7.2,
  "depletion_date": "2026-08-13T18:30:00Z",
  "confidence_level": "low",
  "alert_level": "ok",
  "recommended_topup_ksh": 0
}
```

